1
00:00:07,298 --> 00:00:10,885
I want a Declaration, Roger.
So we can send them in.

2
00:00:10,888 --> 00:00:14,178
- But, Madam President...
- I have the Guard, FEMA and the EPA

3
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:16,889
mobilized and waiting on
the outskirts of that town.

4
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:18,766
I just got off the
phone with the refinery.

5
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:20,895
The leak is well on
its way to burning off.

6
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,814
My understanding is that
the air quality is dangerous.

7
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:27,191
The levels are somewhat elevated, yes,

8
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:30,236
- but the winds are in our favor.
- And subject to change.

9
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:31,904
That's how wind works.

10
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:33,992
This will all be over in a day or two,

11
00:00:33,995 --> 00:00:36,579
the idea of keeping these
families out of their homes...

12
00:00:36,582 --> 00:00:38,744
This is a prudent precaution

13
00:00:38,747 --> 00:00:41,414
and on my watch, that's
what I want to happen.

14
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:43,418
I don't think we should
exaggerate the situation.

15
00:00:46,512 --> 00:00:48,848
Do you remember where you were
on election night, Governor?

16
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,133
Because I do.

17
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,970
You were going to lose.

18
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:58,933
Statistically, there is no
reason you should have won.

19
00:01:02,093 --> 00:01:04,978
Keep the phone away from your mouth
while you're thinking, Governor.

20
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,357
I can hear you breathing.

21
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:08,818
Yes.

22
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:14,824
I do believe I need to
declare a state of emergency.

23
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:19,287
Of course, it's your call.

24
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:22,955
And I assure you, you
will have the full support

25
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:24,292
of the federal government.

26
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:30,379
I promised myself I
wouldn't be like him.

27
00:01:30,381 --> 00:01:32,383
That was textbook Francis, wasn't it?

28
00:01:33,259 --> 00:01:37,178
But he handed me over to
them like a shaker of salt

29
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,807
and now they won't let go.

30
00:01:40,517 --> 00:01:42,936
This is a wound of their own making.

31
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:47,607
Mr. Vice President?

32
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,149
Yeah, come in.

33
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:57,198
Do you need a moment, sir?

34
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,343
No, no.

35
00:01:59,346 --> 00:02:00,870
What is it?

36
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,557
Okay.

37
00:02:10,504 --> 00:02:11,737
Governor?

38
00:03:36,854 --> 00:03:41,267
- <font color="#D81D1D">Synced and corrected by VitoSilans</font> -
-- <font color="#138CE9">www.Addic7ed.com</font> --

39
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:50,645
They said it was fine.

40
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:54,482
It smelled like rotten
eggs and trash. That's all.

41
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:56,901
You could smell it
coming out of the faucet.

42
00:03:56,903 --> 00:04:00,404
And then my son, his... His nose
started to bleed and I thought,

43
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:02,740
- "Is that related?"
- Where is your little boy right now?

44
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:05,370
Now? He's in triage with his mom.

45
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:10,081
- He's my heart, that little guy.
- No, I know. I know.

46
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,666
But, ma'am. If I may. You...

47
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:13,918
You have to tell us.
Is this real or not?

48
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,879
Because at first they said
that we don't need to evacuate,

49
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:18,089
and then all of a sudden that we should.

50
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:20,883
I want you to know everything is
going to be all right. I promise you.

51
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:23,549
We were relying on that
plant to keep us informed.

52
00:04:23,552 --> 00:04:25,390
Sir, you and your safety

53
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,723
is the most important thing.

54
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:30,770
In fact, all of the
families of Bellport,

55
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:33,231
nothing else matters.

56
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:36,983
I want to give my thanks
to Governor Olmstead

57
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:39,360
for his quick and
decisive act this morning

58
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:41,570
in declaring a state of emergency.

59
00:04:41,572 --> 00:04:44,198
We have FEMA, we have EPA,

60
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,367
the Ohio National Guard.

61
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:47,537
They're all here.

62
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:51,374
No one should ever feel unsafe.

63
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,751
In her own home.

64
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:57,213
And how is it you have no idea, Mark?

65
00:04:57,214 --> 00:04:59,797
- It doesn't matter.
- Oh, it does matter.

66
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:02,008
It speaks to this untenable arrangement.

67
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:04,552
Later, I said. Let's stay
focused on our response.

68
00:05:04,554 --> 00:05:06,470
She was all set to sign
the bill this morning.

69
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:08,318
We had photographers, a press
pool waiting, the whole thing.

70
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:09,931
But she didn't sign it, did she?

71
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:11,434
I'm on my way there now.

72
00:05:11,436 --> 00:05:14,895
Because she was too busy manufacturing
an emergency out of nothing.

73
00:05:14,897 --> 00:05:17,565
Look, let's not forget
who escalated this. Okay?

74
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:18,649
Excuse me?

75
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:20,359
If we're working together, Bill,

76
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:22,778
I need to be included in every decision.

77
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:24,655
Every one.

78
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:26,282
This conversation's over.

79
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:28,200
Oh, for God's sakes.

80
00:05:28,202 --> 00:05:29,744
I'll join Annette in Bellport.

81
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:30,942
No, you won't.

82
00:05:30,945 --> 00:05:33,039
One of you showing up
on site is bad enough.

83
00:05:33,041 --> 00:05:34,999
Annette, call me back.

84
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:38,085
Mark.

85
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:39,422
Mark, are you still there?

86
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:42,048
Yes.

87
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,260
Let me talk to him. I'll circle back.

88
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,275
Hello, everyone.

89
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:02,651
My name is Kelsey Stewart.

90
00:06:02,653 --> 00:06:04,570
I'm the deputy press secretary,

91
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:06,699
and I will be taking
your questions today.

92
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:09,033
Sarah.

93
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:11,160
Is it true that Governor
Olmstead was resistant

94
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:13,037
to declaring a state of emergency?

95
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:15,623
The Governor did declare
a state of emergency,

96
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,916
and the White House concurs.

97
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:19,251
Something very wrong
happened in that plant.

98
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:20,294
Yes.

99
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:22,452
Arcas has been slow
to provide any details

100
00:06:22,455 --> 00:06:24,507
when it comes to the leak and explosion.

101
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,550
Not to mention the two
lives lost in the accident.

102
00:06:26,552 --> 00:06:28,969
Have they been cooperating
with the White House?

103
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:30,846
Now that the president is on the ground,

104
00:06:30,848 --> 00:06:33,309
it seems that, yes, they
have been more agreeable.

105
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:36,479
Uh... That's not the
real question, though.

106
00:06:37,271 --> 00:06:40,940
Somebody might want to ask, where
is Shepherd Unlimited in all of this?

107
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:44,161
The Arcas Refinery is a subsidiary
of the family's conglomerate.

108
00:06:44,164 --> 00:06:47,346
Are you saying that the
Shepherds are personally aware

109
00:06:47,349 --> 00:06:49,115
of problems at the plant?

110
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:50,872
Who is responsible and how

111
00:06:50,875 --> 00:06:52,519
is all the White House and the president

112
00:06:52,522 --> 00:06:54,202
are trying to find out at this point.

113
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:56,956
Will this have any effect

114
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:59,333
on the regulatory bill
on the president's desk?

115
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:01,794
The president will be
speaking on that shortly.

116
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:03,045
Marcus.

117
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:06,298
Was the president planning to
divorce the former president

118
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,094
in the days leading up to his death?

119
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:12,807
Uh, let's...

120
00:07:13,641 --> 00:07:15,766
- Oh. Mr. Vice President.
- Morning, everyone.

121
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:18,477
I hope Miss Stewart won't mind
me taking a couple of questions.

122
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:22,230
Mr. Vice President, one question!

123
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:24,024
Marcus, who's your source?

124
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:26,861
- Unnamed officials.
- Nope. We don't do that anymore.

125
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:29,029
We need names. You have a name?

126
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:31,907
I mean really, where do you get this?

127
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:32,910
The former president

128
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,494
spent his last night alive

129
00:07:35,496 --> 00:07:37,246
next to his wife in
the White House. Period.

130
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:38,624
As for Bellport...

131
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,792
let's not jump to conclusions
before all the facts are in.

132
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:43,081
What else?

133
00:07:43,084 --> 00:07:46,086
We still going door to door,
but it's really a precaution.

134
00:07:46,089 --> 00:07:47,715
Are there enough beds?

135
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:51,093
We have a few church basements
and the local jail if we need more.

136
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:54,263
Whatever hydrogen sulfide there is
left in the air is already dissipating.

137
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:56,807
In a day or two, people will be
back sleeping in their own beds.

138
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:58,392
You have to understand,

139
00:07:58,394 --> 00:08:00,060
Madam President,

140
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:03,522
most everyone overreacts
when it comes to chemicals.

141
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:05,274
We have years of experience...

142
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:07,234
And the men who died in the accident?

143
00:08:07,236 --> 00:08:10,654
That's tragic, of course.
They were valued employees.

144
00:08:10,656 --> 00:08:13,782
Members of the community.
There's no way to replace them.

145
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:15,286
And Bill Shepherd?

146
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,164
- Yes.
- Have you heard from him?

147
00:08:19,081 --> 00:08:22,416
I've kept him informed, as
well as all of our partners.

148
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:26,086
Bill called me directly. They're
ready to do whatever's needed.

149
00:08:26,088 --> 00:08:27,546
They're important to Bellport.

150
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:30,257
They built the local stadium. Even
this gymnasium. They contributed...

151
00:08:30,259 --> 00:08:32,384
No, I'm well aware of
the family's philanthropy.

152
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:33,761
That wasn't the question.

153
00:08:33,763 --> 00:08:37,806
Yes, Mr. Shepherd has been
monitoring the situation closely.

154
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:39,435
I would like to tour the area.

155
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:45,022
Is that a problem, Governor?

156
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:47,443
No, no, not to my understanding.

157
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:50,861
I was hoping to get you over to...

158
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:52,530
To where we set up our triage.

159
00:08:52,532 --> 00:08:54,406
It might be best if we
stick to the itinerary...

160
00:08:54,408 --> 00:08:56,242
I'd actually like to see it for myself.

161
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:58,552
Unless, of course,
you tell me otherwise.

162
00:08:58,555 --> 00:08:59,997
No, of course not.

163
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:11,634
The guard marks the
doors of the evacuees.

164
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,387
Pretty standard procedure.

165
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:18,474
Stop the car. I think I see someone.

166
00:09:19,977 --> 00:09:21,227
Stop the car.

167
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:25,354
Madam President, we'll
have someone circle back.

168
00:09:25,356 --> 00:09:26,566
Stop the car now.

169
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:37,118
Damn it.

170
00:09:38,202 --> 00:09:39,785
Is she safe?

171
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:41,998
Nothing is 100% safe.

172
00:09:57,471 --> 00:09:59,098
Hello. Anyone here?

173
00:10:23,607 --> 00:10:25,416
The boy could have lost an eye.

174
00:10:25,419 --> 00:10:26,582
That's not how we treat people.

175
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:28,542
- How could she?
- My God, Elizabeth, stop it.

176
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:30,169
Am I raising a daughter or an animal?

177
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:32,254
They're the animals, the
way they attacked her.

178
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:34,840
Oh, of course, take her side. Of course!

179
00:10:34,842 --> 00:10:36,967
It's time she learned about the world.

180
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:40,306
Pretty girls have a
responsibility to their beauty.

181
00:10:41,098 --> 00:10:43,641
I'll bet she dared those boys.

182
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:44,769
Shame on her.

183
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:48,814
Why can't you just do as you're told?

184
00:10:49,981 --> 00:10:51,356
Why, indeed?

185
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:54,278
Madam President! Madam President.

186
00:10:57,573 --> 00:10:58,908
Madam President...

187
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:02,411
might be best if we head back.

188
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:04,861
So, the house is safe?

189
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:14,882
Drink it then.

190
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:23,891
I thought so.

191
00:11:46,121 --> 00:11:49,080
- But what am I agreeing to?
- I can read it for you.

192
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,648
I can read.

193
00:11:50,651 --> 00:11:52,044
And what's this for?

194
00:11:53,003 --> 00:11:56,213
That lets the app figure out
how we can be most helpful.

195
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:59,633
It can be tailored to your specific
needs. We want to keep you informed.

196
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:02,845
We want you to know what
happens before it happens.

197
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,722
You can't trust the
government to do that.

198
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:07,015
- Hello, my name is Seth Grayson.
- Nice to meet you.

199
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:10,060
I'm with Shepherd Freedom Foundation,
can I talk to you for a second?

200
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:14,191
Sure thing. I was looking at
the pamphlet saying just...

201
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:21,198
It's the president.

202
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:48,184
Madam President.

203
00:12:49,518 --> 00:12:52,062
Whose idea was it? To
leave it on his bed?

204
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:54,106
Not here.

205
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:58,903
The Shepherd Freedom
Foundation is here to help.

206
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:03,661
The federal government
is here to help you.

207
00:13:03,664 --> 00:13:05,365
Yes, Madam President.

208
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:09,349
The only way America's problems
will be solved is through alliances

209
00:13:09,364 --> 00:13:13,099
between government and private
industry, each doing its part.

210
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:17,753
The Commander in Chief
and I go way back.

211
00:13:17,755 --> 00:13:20,297
We do. And I know I
have the full cooperation

212
00:13:20,299 --> 00:13:21,673
from the Shepherd family.

213
00:13:21,675 --> 00:13:26,011
The blatant disregard for human life
exhibited by companies like Arcas...

214
00:13:26,013 --> 00:13:29,014
Arcas is committed to
the safety of its workers.

215
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:31,475
And with the help of...

216
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:34,231
the right kind of legislation,
like the FUTURE Act.

217
00:13:34,234 --> 00:13:36,357
Which is under review at the moment.

218
00:13:37,024 --> 00:13:38,607
Until then,

219
00:13:38,609 --> 00:13:42,486
I am hereby moving the EPA's
Criminal Investigative Division

220
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,488
into the Pentagon,

221
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:48,867
where it will enjoy the forces
and the resources of our military.

222
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:51,205
And they will investigate this disaster.

223
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:55,751
I swear on my husband's grave, I
will find out what happened here.

224
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:58,671
Thank you for your support.

225
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:03,893
I wanted to leave it on your bed.

226
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:10,615
Don't be thick, thick I can't use.

227
00:14:10,618 --> 00:14:12,891
Did she actually ask for a divorce?

228
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:15,936
- As if that matters.
- And if I'm asked to justify the question?

229
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:18,910
It was justified the moment
they didn't have an answer.

230
00:14:18,913 --> 00:14:21,443
The last thing the president
wants is to be talking

231
00:14:21,444 --> 00:14:22,910
about the former president.

232
00:14:22,913 --> 00:14:24,167
Let me ask you this.

233
00:14:24,170 --> 00:14:25,404
How did your mother feel

234
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:27,739
when the president yanked
her hand away like that?

235
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:30,285
That's none of your
goddamn business, Marcus.

236
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:34,903
Recoil? Is that the word you used?

237
00:14:34,905 --> 00:14:36,123
Yeah, that's what I see.

238
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,374
- Are you kidding me?
- No.

239
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:40,586
Are we really gonna waste time
dissecting a gesture between two women?

240
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:42,796
Nora's right. I was there.
There wasn't a recoil.

241
00:14:42,798 --> 00:14:44,464
I gotta agree with Tom here. For me,

242
00:14:44,466 --> 00:14:46,758
it's Annette Shepherd sort
of manhandling the president

243
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:49,553
as a sign of victory, and
then I detect a flinch.

244
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:51,847
A slight flinch, then recoil.

245
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:54,182
- Recoil? I mean...
- She's trying to separate herself

246
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:57,183
from the primary source of
the funding for what was to be

247
00:14:57,186 --> 00:15:00,312
- the Francis J. Underwood Foundation.
- This is about culpability.

248
00:15:00,315 --> 00:15:03,482
She went to Bellport to hold
those responsible accountable.

249
00:15:03,485 --> 00:15:06,737
Companies like Shepherd
Unlimited have been hamstrung.

250
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,864
And that's why this bill
on her desk is so important.

251
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:11,909
Legislation means nothing
without proper enforcement.

252
