507
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:14,359
I'd slip my hand into a coat
pocket to see what I could find.

508
00:28:15,735 --> 00:28:18,613
A stranger's pocket is
a window into his soul.

509
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:21,783
And what did you find?

510
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:25,201
Condoms.

511
00:28:25,203 --> 00:28:27,622
Mints. Keys.

512
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:31,000
Did you steal what you found?

513
00:28:31,918 --> 00:28:34,419
Not the mints. Because
that would be cruel.

514
00:28:36,923 --> 00:28:37,966
Was that you...

515
00:28:39,467 --> 00:28:40,800
on the way to the airport?

516
00:28:40,802 --> 00:28:43,177
Were you trying to teach her a lesson?

517
00:28:43,179 --> 00:28:44,554
- Talk to Bill.
- Come on.

518
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:46,099
I already did.

519
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:52,145
- She's late.
- Yeah, she's the president.

520
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:54,856
You know, you have a
weakness for strong women.

521
00:28:54,858 --> 00:28:55,940
Oh.

522
00:28:55,942 --> 00:28:56,943
No, really.

523
00:28:59,028 --> 00:29:00,739
You think they need your help.

524
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:08,202
Really?

525
00:29:08,204 --> 00:29:09,998
- Still?
- No, no.

526
00:29:10,707 --> 00:29:11,916
I chew now.

527
00:29:12,664 --> 00:29:14,336
I just like to...

528
00:29:14,339 --> 00:29:15,680
play with this.

529
00:29:18,256 --> 00:29:20,008
Wait.

530
00:29:23,073 --> 00:29:24,304
She's here.

531
00:29:46,159 --> 00:29:48,828
Madam President, Duncan Shepherd.

532
00:29:49,662 --> 00:29:52,081
- Oh. Hello.
- Claire.

533
00:29:53,103 --> 00:29:54,759
Annette.

534
00:29:54,762 --> 00:29:56,711
I see you've met Duncan.

535
00:29:57,587 --> 00:29:59,464
- Shall we?
- Yes.

536
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:06,930
Don't ever recoil from me again.

537
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:21,611
- Ain't 50 nifty?
- Mm-hmm.

538
00:30:22,654 --> 00:30:25,321
I think the last time you
dragged me into a bathroom,

539
00:30:25,323 --> 00:30:27,323
it was to show off your hickey.

540
00:30:31,079 --> 00:30:33,623
I don't think your brother
is gonna let up, Annette.

541
00:30:34,415 --> 00:30:37,252
Until he gets his ring
kissed directly, I think.

542
00:30:39,254 --> 00:30:41,712
Reminds me of someone
you were married to.

543
00:30:41,714 --> 00:30:45,550
Oh, no. Bill and Francis
are very different people.

544
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:46,553
Agreed.

545
00:30:49,264 --> 00:30:51,099
You know I slept with him once.

546
00:30:51,975 --> 00:30:53,951
Your brother?

547
00:30:53,954 --> 00:30:55,228
Your husband.

548
00:30:56,584 --> 00:30:57,856
I know.

549
00:30:59,524 --> 00:31:00,859
Interesting.

550
00:31:01,609 --> 00:31:03,736
Though, come to think of
it, I guess it makes sense.

551
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:06,553
What does?

552
00:31:07,448 --> 00:31:09,868
That your marriage allowed for that.

553
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:14,078
Well, it was the '98 campaign.

554
00:31:14,080 --> 00:31:17,081
Francis was facing a robust challenger,

555
00:31:17,083 --> 00:31:20,334
and there you were at some
DC fundraiser or other.

556
00:31:20,336 --> 00:31:22,128
It was at the Union Station,

557
00:31:22,130 --> 00:31:23,212
- East Hall.
- Yes.

558
00:31:23,214 --> 00:31:24,934
And there you were,
dangling your checkbook.

559
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:28,259
So, it sounds like a favorable
transaction all around.

560
00:31:28,261 --> 00:31:31,596
- Is that what he told you?
- I never asked for details.

561
00:31:31,598 --> 00:31:33,472
I mean, I was curious.

562
00:31:33,474 --> 00:31:35,558
I really was.

563
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,226
He was a good kisser, I'll say that.

564
00:31:37,228 --> 00:31:41,230
But then the rest was so underwhelming.

565
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:43,524
Felt like he wasn't all there.

566
00:31:43,526 --> 00:31:44,694
Like, he wasn't...

567
00:31:45,361 --> 00:31:46,821
all in, so to speak.

568
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:49,824
Of course, my first thought, and...

569
00:31:50,950 --> 00:31:52,325
isn't this true of most women?

570
00:31:52,327 --> 00:31:53,910
Was to wonder if it was me.

571
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:58,791
Was I somehow less skilled
than I like to believe I am?

572
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:02,545
Well, I can't really
answer to that, Annette.

573
00:32:03,254 --> 00:32:04,878
I can.

574
00:32:04,881 --> 00:32:06,007
It was him.

575
00:32:07,941 --> 00:32:09,177
And...

576
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:12,513
I bet it was never
very different with you.

577
00:32:14,307 --> 00:32:15,932
Even you.

578
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:17,477
The blonde goddess.

579
00:32:18,186 --> 00:32:20,772
Even with you. Am I right?

580
00:32:23,178 --> 00:32:24,484
Wow.

581
00:32:26,027 --> 00:32:28,112
It's really only dawning on me now.

582
00:32:28,988 --> 00:32:30,740
The sacrifice you made.

583
00:32:32,325 --> 00:32:33,866
I sort of pity you.

584
00:32:33,868 --> 00:32:37,453
What you must have denied
yourself all those years.

585
00:32:37,455 --> 00:32:40,375
And this is where I tell you
to shut your mouth, Annette.

586
00:32:41,459 --> 00:32:44,001
You don't know anything about marriage,

587
00:32:44,003 --> 00:32:45,129
much less mine.

588
00:32:46,339 --> 00:32:48,716
Tell yourself whatever you want, Claire.

589
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:51,052
We both know the truth.

590
00:32:52,261 --> 00:32:54,472
He's waiting for you down
the hall in the prep kitchen.

591
00:32:57,350 --> 00:32:58,351
My brother.

592
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:02,021
I can still do it by the way.

593
00:33:03,900 --> 00:33:05,252
Can you?

594
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:00,277
Well, you missed dinner.

595
00:34:01,456 --> 00:34:03,289
I can have 'em make
you whatever you like.

596
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:04,375
I'm not hungry.

597
00:34:05,334 --> 00:34:07,126
The secret here is how much

598
00:34:07,128 --> 00:34:08,713
lemon juice you put in.

599
00:34:09,338 --> 00:34:10,840
Balance out the butter.

600
00:34:12,050 --> 00:34:13,966
People and hollandaise.

601
00:34:13,968 --> 00:34:15,678
They think it tastes like money.

602
00:34:16,512 --> 00:34:19,388
- A night at the hotel.
- What where you looking for?

603
00:34:19,390 --> 00:34:22,310
There's nothing in the
Gaffney home of value.

604
00:34:24,687 --> 00:34:26,246
Frank did things.

605
00:34:26,249 --> 00:34:27,607
And you just, what?

606
00:34:28,357 --> 00:34:29,523
Look the other way?

607
00:34:29,525 --> 00:34:32,904
That shot you took at me, it's
not like you to be so reckless.

608
00:34:33,905 --> 00:34:35,281
You don't scare easy.

609
00:34:36,657 --> 00:34:41,120
The future of our country is at stake.

610
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:43,331
Does that sound...

611
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,750
pat to you, naive?

612
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:48,086
No, not at all.

613
00:34:48,886 --> 00:34:51,428
Do you think I don't have
friends at the Pentagon, Claire?

614
00:34:51,431 --> 00:34:54,965
You may want to make my four
years in office miserable...

615
00:34:54,967 --> 00:34:57,676
All I want you to do
is behave, as promised.

616
00:34:57,678 --> 00:35:01,180
You can dig up a ring or whatever
else you can get your hands on.

617
00:35:01,182 --> 00:35:05,019
But that doesn't mean I won't make
your time a living hell as well.

618
00:35:09,148 --> 00:35:11,649
Raymond Tusk said about you one time,

619
00:35:11,651 --> 00:35:13,400
some dinner we were
at, he just said it...

620
00:35:13,402 --> 00:35:15,528
This is where I'm supposed to be
a little bit afraid of the answer,

621
00:35:15,530 --> 00:35:16,987
- I suppose.
- He said, "I don't know,

622
00:35:16,989 --> 00:35:18,699
whether or not she's a person...

623
00:35:20,510 --> 00:35:22,409
or just playing the part of one."

624
00:35:22,411 --> 00:35:26,697
And I thought it was so strange
at the time, but maybe it's true.

625
00:35:26,700 --> 00:35:27,959
Just...

626
00:35:30,545 --> 00:35:32,028
unreachable.

627
00:35:34,966 --> 00:35:36,509
I know it'll be hard for you.

628
00:35:38,052 --> 00:35:40,304
But you're going to have to
treat me as an equal, Bill.

629
00:35:44,267 --> 00:35:46,018
What did you do with
your husband's will?

630
00:35:46,853 --> 00:35:49,040
It was a revocable trust.

631
00:35:49,043 --> 00:35:50,312
All done.

632
00:35:50,314 --> 00:35:52,066
I'm not talking about that one.

633
00:35:53,109 --> 00:35:55,276
I'm talking about the other one.

634
00:35:55,278 --> 00:35:56,362
The new one.

635
00:35:57,426 --> 00:36:01,222
Bet Doug Stamper would love to
see the contents of that one.

636
00:36:02,618 --> 00:36:03,911
What's in there anyway?

637
00:36:04,620 --> 00:36:08,454
That you would go to such lengths

638
00:36:08,457 --> 00:36:09,876
to keep him from it?

639
00:36:13,629 --> 00:36:15,214
Claire Hale has a secret.

640
00:36:19,677 --> 00:36:23,637
Douglas Stamper is meeting
with the US District Attorney

641
00:36:23,639 --> 00:36:24,974
as we speak.

642
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:27,351
He's out, Claire.

643
00:36:28,477 --> 00:36:30,313
And he's not going back in.

644
00:36:31,981 --> 00:36:34,317
Now, you need my help.

645
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:36,652
Later tonight,

646
00:36:37,862 --> 00:36:41,155
I'm going to watch you sign that bill

647
00:36:41,157 --> 00:36:43,159
that's sitting on your desk.

648
00:36:44,618 --> 00:36:46,159
"To the dead,

649
00:36:46,162 --> 00:36:48,289
a kingdom means nothing.

650
00:36:49,332 --> 00:36:52,376
They have their requiem and eternity."

651
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:55,731
That's Macbeth. The opera, not the play.

652
00:36:56,631 --> 00:36:59,506
All you have to do now
is just go on out there

653
00:36:59,508 --> 00:37:01,510
with your oldest, dearest friend and...

654
00:37:03,012 --> 00:37:04,931
hold her hand up high.

655
00:37:20,321 --> 00:37:21,820
Madam President.

656
00:37:21,822 --> 00:37:24,823
You don't really think
the military is irrelevant?

657
00:37:24,825 --> 00:37:29,954
I watched your confirmation
from my chambers for the UN.

658
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:33,040
- Wasn't my finest hour.
- Well, he who laughs loudest...

659
00:37:33,042 --> 00:37:34,917
Or is it "laughs last"?

660
00:37:34,919 --> 00:37:37,169
"Last." "She."

661
00:37:37,171 --> 00:37:39,588
- Vincent Abruzzo.
- Ninth Circuit.

662
00:37:39,590 --> 00:37:41,924
I am no good at functions like this.

663
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:45,063
I tend to find a chair at these things

664
00:37:45,066 --> 00:37:47,096
and sit in it for the
rest of the evening.

665
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:49,640
- Madam President.
- Yes. Well, it's been a pleasure.

666
00:37:49,642 --> 00:37:51,892
Madam President, if I may say,

667
00:37:51,894 --> 00:37:55,562
I'm so glad that we finally
have a woman in the Oval Office.

668
00:37:55,564 --> 00:37:58,607
The arc of history is long, but...

669
00:37:58,609 --> 00:38:01,279
The reign of the middle-aged
white man is over.

670
00:38:01,904 --> 00:38:05,283
The Bill Shepherds of the world
who won't let go, have to go.

671
00:38:12,748 --> 00:38:16,458
Does anyone except you know about
the document that came for him?

672
00:38:16,460 --> 00:38:17,837
No, of course not.

673
00:38:18,921 --> 00:38:21,297
Because if anyone else gets
their hand on that will...

674
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:23,173
That is strictly between us.

675
00:38:23,175 --> 00:38:25,374
We only just discovered
that he was missing.

676
00:38:25,377 --> 00:38:28,304
I put a call into the US
Attorney and was just informed

677
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:29,765
charges have been dropped.

678
00:38:30,641 --> 00:38:32,099
How is that even possible?

679
00:38:32,101 --> 00:38:34,645
I thought I'd lost my phone
a couple of days ago, but...

680
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:38,607
But now I'm certain that he took
it and reached out to make a deal.

681
00:38:39,525 --> 00:38:41,608
I can have a grand jury impaneled

682
00:38:41,610 --> 00:38:44,780
and we can be taking testimony
from witnesses within a week.

683
00:38:46,657 --> 00:38:47,700
Who do you have?

684
00:38:48,451 --> 00:38:49,827
Secretary Durant?

685
00:38:51,787 --> 00:38:52,788
And others.

686
00:38:55,041 --> 00:38:58,876
I'm sure I don't need to talk to
you about what's right or wrong.

687
00:38:58,878 --> 00:39:01,587
But in my experience,
most people, in the end,

688
00:39:01,589 --> 00:39:03,758
will do whatever they need
to, to save themselves.

689
00:39:12,516 --> 00:39:14,560
Do you think you have
a strong enough case?

690
00:39:15,353 --> 00:39:16,729
That depends on you.

691
00:39:17,396 --> 00:39:20,856
If I'm gonna put myself on the line,
I need to know you're going to win.

692
00:39:20,858 --> 00:39:22,858
This can be a very unforgiving town.

693
00:39:22,860 --> 00:39:24,570
I'm giving you a chance to start over.

694
00:39:26,947 --> 00:39:29,073
- Come on.
- I can offer you immunity

695
00:39:29,075 --> 00:39:30,242
for your testimony.

696
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:34,536
But, Mr. Stamper, of course,
I can't give you any guarantees

697
00:39:34,538 --> 00:39:37,792
when it comes to your reputation
or that of the former president.

698
00:39:38,834 --> 00:39:40,961
You would have to
testify in an open court.

699
00:39:41,712 --> 00:39:42,713
That is the deal.

700
00:39:48,803 --> 00:39:50,554
I should consult with my lawyers.

701
00:39:53,808 --> 00:39:55,643
Thank you for your time, Mr. Stamper.

702
00:40:06,018 --> 00:40:08,940
Join us in supporting the
Dallas Scholarship Fund

703
00:40:08,943 --> 00:40:10,234
for Young Women:

704
00:40:10,237 --> 00:40:11,322
Take aim.

705
00:40:26,257 --> 00:40:29,007
Look at these marvelous faces.

706
00:40:29,009 --> 00:40:31,053
The faces of our future.

707
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:35,013
And I am so, so honored

708
00:40:35,015 --> 00:40:37,933
to be chosen to introduce to you

709
00:40:37,935 --> 00:40:41,355
the President of the United
States, Claire Underwood.

710
00:41:07,715 --> 00:41:10,296
I look at these brilliant young women

711
00:41:10,299 --> 00:41:11,967
and words fail me.

712
00:41:14,930 --> 00:41:16,263
What's this?

713
00:41:16,265 --> 00:41:18,974
They gave us these.
What are they gonna do?

714
00:41:18,976 --> 00:41:20,767
Yeah, I'm not drinking the water,

715
00:41:20,769 --> 00:41:22,769
no fucking way, I'll tell you that.

716
00:41:22,771 --> 00:41:25,355
I'll go all the way to Canton
to buy it, if I have to.

717
00:41:25,357 --> 00:41:27,693
And... Mr. Grayson,

718
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:30,903
what else did he tell you about the app?

719
00:41:30,905 --> 00:41:34,239
Nothing. You can go
online and check it out.

720
00:41:34,241 --> 00:41:37,659
'Cause a lot of people I know signed
up for it even after the president left.

721
00:41:37,662 --> 00:41:39,043
Hmm.

722
00:41:41,739 --> 00:41:43,000
He said...

723
00:41:45,002 --> 00:41:46,286
Mr. Grayson?

724
00:41:48,047 --> 00:41:49,298
Yeah, him.

725
00:41:50,466 --> 00:41:52,591
That they were gonna tell
us what was gonna happen

726
00:41:52,593 --> 00:41:54,220
- before it happens.
- How?

727
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:58,140
Look, I don't know.

728
00:41:59,099 --> 00:42:01,560
Ithaca's, like, where?

729
00:42:02,686 --> 00:42:04,436
There's one in Greece.

730
00:42:04,438 --> 00:42:06,315
And the other's in upstate New York.

731
00:42:07,441 --> 00:42:08,857
Guess which one I'm from.

732
00:42:13,739 --> 00:42:16,242
It's a paper, it comes out once a week.

733
00:42:24,124 --> 00:42:25,251
It was going to happen,

734
00:42:26,085 --> 00:42:27,336
because it happened before.

735
00:42:28,254 --> 00:42:30,638
We complained all the
way to the EPA, but...

736
00:42:30,641 --> 00:42:31,924
whatever.

737
00:42:32,925 --> 00:42:35,050
Only this time the explosion was bad.

738
00:42:35,052 --> 00:42:38,764
And yeah, some guys died.
And the company knew.

739
00:42:40,678 --> 00:42:41,934
They knew.

740
00:42:54,405 --> 00:42:55,614
Welcome home.

741
00:43:06,959 --> 00:43:09,295
Good timing. I just put on coffee.

742
00:43:10,462 --> 00:43:11,745
A little late for coffee.

743
00:43:11,748 --> 00:43:13,757
Well, we have so much to talk about.

744
00:43:15,758 --> 00:43:17,341
I'm glad you're out, Doug.

745
00:43:17,344 --> 00:43:19,386
I don't know what you
were doing in there.

746
00:43:21,316 --> 00:43:22,859
How's the US Attorney?

747
00:43:27,146 --> 00:43:29,565
Secretary Durant's
negotiating her appearance.

748
00:43:32,151 --> 00:43:33,817
And if...

749
00:43:33,819 --> 00:43:36,695
Cathy should somehow be dissuaded?

750
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:39,033
- Silenced?
- Then it all goes away.

751
00:43:40,492 --> 00:43:42,411
Yes, but they'll still want to know

752
00:43:43,037 --> 00:43:44,830
who knew what, when.

753
00:43:47,416 --> 00:43:48,626
I feel pretty clear.

754
00:43:51,378 --> 00:43:53,420
You think it was me who
asked you to take the fall

755
00:43:53,422 --> 00:43:56,590
- just because I said the words, right?
- He told me it was you.

756
00:43:56,592 --> 00:43:59,009
- He whispered it in my ear.
- And you believed him.

757
00:43:59,011 --> 00:44:00,346
Like you always believed him.

758
00:44:01,930 --> 00:44:05,182
Well, here's what I believe.
Zoe Barnes killed herself...

759
00:44:05,184 --> 00:44:07,476
And I expected to be
pardoned for the rest.

760
00:44:07,478 --> 00:44:10,062
Since his death, my
hands have been tied.

761
00:44:11,315 --> 00:44:13,817
But I believe the universe
has given us a gift.

762
00:44:15,861 --> 00:44:17,363
I don't know what that means.

763
00:44:18,202 --> 00:44:19,406
Well...

764
00:44:21,116 --> 00:44:23,356
We both lost someone

765
00:44:23,359 --> 00:44:26,085
who shaped the course of our lives.

766
00:44:26,088 --> 00:44:28,832
For good, but also for ill.

767
00:44:30,125 --> 00:44:31,543
And now here we are

768
00:44:32,586 --> 00:44:34,213
unexpectedly free.

769
00:44:36,131 --> 00:44:37,549
To take a different tack.

770
00:44:41,845 --> 00:44:43,931
We can do whatever we want, Doug.

771
00:44:45,974 --> 00:44:48,433
And we've been entwined, you and I,

772
00:44:48,435 --> 00:44:49,436
like it or not,

773
00:44:50,145 --> 00:44:51,937
for decades now.

774
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:53,023
But I think...

775
00:44:54,233 --> 00:44:56,193
we deserve to go our separate ways.

776
00:44:57,778 --> 00:45:01,865
The only problem is we have something
urgent to attend to called Cathy Durant.

777
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:06,078
And then we can finally be free.

778
00:45:08,455 --> 00:45:09,998
Do what we really want.

779
00:45:10,833 --> 00:45:12,251
Do what we need to do.

780
00:45:15,879 --> 00:45:17,756
What does Doug Stamper want?

781
00:45:18,716 --> 00:45:20,592
Are you trying to erase him?

782
00:45:22,428 --> 00:45:23,762
Because you can't.

783
00:45:24,430 --> 00:45:26,092
I'm not trying to do anything

784
00:45:26,095 --> 00:45:28,722
except be the sitting
President of the United States.

785
00:45:30,811 --> 00:45:32,730
It's wrong to assume

786
00:45:33,647 --> 00:45:36,650
Francis's ambitions directly
aligned with mine, Doug.

787
00:45:38,152 --> 00:45:42,112
The best way to not to be associated
with his questionable deeds

788
00:45:42,114 --> 00:45:44,034
is to do good. That's
what I plan to do, anyway.

789
00:45:50,664 --> 00:45:52,867
Oh, you find that funny, do you?

790
00:45:52,870 --> 00:45:54,293
Well, it's true.

791
00:45:59,882 --> 00:46:02,134
I never understood what he saw in you.

792
00:46:03,177 --> 00:46:04,720
I mean the outside, sure.

793
00:46:06,138 --> 00:46:07,306
But the inside...

794
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:10,726
- LeAnn's death.
- No.

795
00:46:12,144 --> 00:46:13,477
You never cared for her.

796
00:46:13,479 --> 00:46:14,980
It wasn't necessary.

797
00:46:15,981 --> 00:46:17,274
And I told him so.

798
00:46:18,233 --> 00:46:19,318
And yet...

799
00:46:26,950 --> 00:46:28,494
Doug, do me a favor.

800
00:46:33,624 --> 00:46:34,792
Close your eyes.

801
00:46:36,752 --> 00:46:37,753
Please.

802
00:46:50,057 --> 00:46:51,642
He wanted you to have them.

803
00:47:37,020 --> 00:47:39,896
For this to happen at
this point in your life,

804
00:47:39,898 --> 00:47:41,817
the prognosis is not good.

805
00:47:43,819 --> 00:47:44,903
I know.

806
00:47:56,623 --> 00:47:58,540
Somebody killed Francis,

807
00:47:58,542 --> 00:48:00,335
and yet they don't want him to die.

808
00:48:01,086 --> 00:48:03,962
That last night, the last time we spoke,

809
00:48:03,964 --> 00:48:06,675
was when I declined his
phone call in the Oval Office.

810
00:48:07,718 --> 00:48:11,803
It had been close to two months,
and he was tired of waiting.

811
00:48:11,805 --> 00:48:14,764
So he showed up here in the White House.

812
00:48:14,766 --> 00:48:16,059
Like a thief.

813
00:48:16,685 --> 00:48:18,061
It was terrifying.

814
00:48:19,021 --> 00:48:21,026
He was furious, slurring his words.

815
00:48:21,029 --> 00:48:23,567
"Why can't you do as
you're told, Claire?"

816
00:48:25,193 --> 00:48:28,445
I told the world that
he died in our bed,

817
00:48:28,447 --> 00:48:30,196
but that's not the truth.

818
00:48:30,198 --> 00:48:32,407
I locked myself in my room that night,

819
00:48:32,409 --> 00:48:34,912
woke up in the morning
and found him dead in his.

820
00:48:37,497 --> 00:48:39,333
They killed him to shut me up.

821
00:48:41,335 --> 00:48:44,546
I need to bury Francis,
once and for all.

822
00:49:05,025 --> 00:49:07,319
Do you need help signing it?

823
00:49:16,203 --> 00:49:18,413
No. Bill. Shepherd, enough.

824
00:49:20,791 --> 00:49:22,668
I actually have one condition.

825
00:49:25,921 --> 00:49:27,467
Put it back.

826
00:49:59,389 --> 00:50:09,389
